{% doc %}
  @description Wraps POST /v4/records/{recordId}/documents (Accela "Create Record Documents").

    Accela requires multipart/form-data with two parts: `uploadedFile`
    (the file) and `fileInfo` (a JSON string array of metadata). This is
    sent via `api_call_send`'s inline `form_data` support
    (graphql/accela_client/multipart_upload.graphql,  called from
    lib/accela_client/send.liquid) - platformOS fetches and streams the
    file server-side from a URL, so this module never downloads or holds
    the file's bytes itself unless you give it `file_content_base64`
    instead. Identify the file one of three ways:
    - `file_url`: any URL platformOS's servers can fetch directly.
    - `file_content_base64`: the file's own bytes, base64-encoded, when
      you have them in hand rather than a fetchable URL.
    - `file_object_id`/`file_object_property`: a platformOS generic_object
      record and the file property on it holding an already-uploaded
      file - see those params below for why this is the retry-safe option.

    Follows the pos-module-core build/check/execute command pattern (see
    upload/{build,check}.liquid): build prepares the request URL and the
    `fileInfo` body, check validates required params, and this file
    executes the request itself once valid (rather than delegating to a
    separate execute.liquid).
  @param {string} record_id - Record id (required)
  @param {string} [file_url] - URL of the file to upload; required unless
    `file_content_base64` or `file_object_id`/`file_object_property` are
    given instead.
  @param {string} [file_content_base64] - base64-encoded file content, as
    an alternative to `file_url`.
  @param {string} file_name - Original file name, e.g. "site_plan.pdf"
  @param {string} content_type - MIME type, e.g. "application/pdf" (required)
  @param {string} [category] - must match a value from documents/categories
  @param {string} [description] - description string
  @param {object} [reference] - hash `{ "id", "table" }` forwarded to
    send.liquid - see send.liquid.
  @param {boolean} [with_retries] - default false. When true, retries a
    failed attempt in the background with increasing delay - see
    lib/accela_client/send.liquid. Only meaningful when
    `file_object_id`/`file_object_property` are also given (see below) -
    a directly-passed `file_url` may be a short-lived signed URL that's
    no longer valid by the time a retry fires, and `file_content_base64`
    isn't carried through the retry chain at all (see send.liquid).
  @param {string} [file_object_id] - optional, given together with
    file_object_property, as an alternative to `file_url`/`file_content_base64`.
    Identifies a platformOS generic_object record and the file property on
    it holding this upload's file. Forwarded to send.liquid as
    `metadata.file_object_id`/`metadata.file_object_property` - when both
    are present, send.liquid resolves a fresh signed URL from that
    generic_object before every attempt (this call and any retries)
    instead of relying on a single `file_url` staying valid. This is what
    makes `with_retries` viable for a MULTIPART upload - see
    lib/accela_client/send.liquid.
  @param {string} [file_object_property] - optional, given together with
    file_object_id - see file_object_id above.
  @example
    {% function result = 'modules/accela_construct/commands/records/documents/upload',
       record_id: record_id, file_url: file_url, file_name: 'site_plan.pdf',
       content_type: 'application/pdf', description: 'Site plan' %}
{% enddoc %}

{% liquid
  assign object = { "errors": {}, "valid": true, "record_id": record_id, "file_url": file_url, "file_content_base64": file_content_base64, "file_object_id": file_object_id, "file_object_property": file_object_property, "file_name": file_name, "content_type": content_type, "category": category, "description": description }
  function object = 'modules/accela_construct/commands/records/documents/upload/build', object: object
  function object = 'modules/accela_construct/commands/records/documents/upload/check', object: object

  if object.valid
    assign metadata = { "file_object_id": file_object_id, "file_object_property": file_object_property }
    function result = 'modules/accela_construct/accela_client/send', method: 'MULTIPART', path: object.path, file_url: object.file_url, file_content_base64: object.file_content_base64, file_name: object.file_name, content_type: object.content_type, file_info: object.file_info, reference: reference, caller: 'modules/accela_construct/commands/records/documents/upload', with_retries: with_retries, metadata: metadata
  else
    function result = 'modules/accela_construct/accela_client/error_result', error: 'accela_validation_failed', errors: object.errors, caller: 'modules/accela_construct/commands/records/documents/upload'
  endif

  return result
%}
